  "findings": [
    {
      "claim": "ServerChunkCache.syncLoad has zero frames in both lab.5 and lab.6 captures. In lab.6 Topology.scan is 21 inclusive sampled ms and all CraftBlock.setBlockData contexts total 56 ms.",
      "scope": "Supports continued absence of the previously measured sync-neighbour waits in captured slow ticks; it does not prove that no synchronous load ever happened in unsampled ticks."
    },
    {
      "claim": "PaperweightFaweAdapter.init has zero active frames in lab.6, versus 878 inclusive sampled ms in lab.5. Runtime reports successful warmup costing 640.717487 ms before the active benchmark.",
      "scope": "The observed cold registry work was moved into disclosed setup. Warmup elapsed time and sampled inclusive time are different measurements and are not expected to match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "EditSession.close/flushQueue totals 296 inclusive sampled ms, versus 1298 in lab.5; HeightmapProcessor is 45 versus 953 and PaperweightGetBlocks.update is 13 versus 918.",
      "scope": "Consistent with removal of the sampled cold registry branch; no paired workload speedup factor is claimed."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Remaining pasteBlock work totals 827 inclusive sampled ms. Edit-session creation totals 243; a different cold path is Schematic.lambda$pasteBlock$0 -> CraftBlockData.createBlockState -> CraftBlockStates.<clinit>, totaling 198 ms in the first bucket.",
      "scope": "The registry conversion prewarm did not promise to initialize all detached BlockState classes or all FAWE subsystems. These costs are observed, not attributed to the exact 680 ms tick."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Relighter postProcessChunks totals 320 inclusive sampled ms; sendChunk 313 includes ClientboundLevelChunkWithLightPacket construction 276 ms.",
      "scope": "This is packet construction and postprocessing visible on main; it is not evidence of network delivery time or a synchronous chunk-load wait."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Other residual paths include vanilla entity ticks 551, scheduled ticks 315, chunk unloads 297, ticket updates 245 and native GC_active 357 inclusive sampled ms.",
      "scope": "Overlapping sampled contexts, not additive phase durations. The GC marker is not an exact pause duration and does not identify the sole cause of the maximum tick."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Active maximum is 680.467089 ms, p 99 62.389121 ms and p 95 28.986539 ms; lab.5 was 2759.14109/59.383742/27.5356 ms.",
      "scope": "The observed maximum is lower, but percentiles did not uniformly improve and different structures/coordinates prevent a paired performance conclusion. Remaining >50 ms ticks are explicit."
    },
    {
      "claim": "All 16 origins and 256 zero-write probe receipts completed;10 BuildPlace and 10 PasteComplete events were observed. Coordinator completed 26 jobs,75 requests/75 loaded and 144 holds acquired/released with zero failures/aborts and no remaining activity or tickets.",
      "scope": "Liveness and cleanup observed for this run only. Native request max 44.473731 ms and pin max 11.30233 ms remain unpreemptible measured API calls."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Only Server thread and ticks over 50 ms were sampled. Worker work and unsampled ticks are outside this tree.",
    "First-minute stacks and 680.467089 ms maximum share a bucket but do not have exact per-tick correlation. No single-stack explanation of the entire worst tick is claimed.",
    "Call-tree references, unique reachability, per-window nonnegative self weights and root/self conservation all pass; the separate one-tick metadata/statistics mismatch is retained.",
    "Partial/native roots exist; unknown frames are not reconstructed or assigned to a plugin.",
    "Different natural workloads and capture lengths make raw sample totals unsuitable as paired speedup percentages.",
    "Startup entity and FAWE warmups, readiness wait, idle baseline and active benchmark have distinct scopes.",
    "This task performed no source changes, live commands, activation, reload or restart. No further optimization or run is proposed in this bounded assessment."
  ]
